  "term": "family of origin",
  "definition": "Family of origin refers to the family environment a person grows up in, which is described here as having a major influence on development and lifelong mental health. It includes both risk and protective influences such as genetics, family conditions, parental wellbeing, the parents’ relationship, parenting style, and the parent-child relationship.",
